<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Norman invasion of Ireland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1169–1171</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Norman invasion of Ireland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Norman invasion of Ireland began in 1169, when Norman knights from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> landed to support the deposed king of Leinster, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a>. Led from 1170 by Richard de Clare, known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke">Strongbow</a>, they took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>, and in 1171 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> came to Ireland and received the submission of many Irish kings. It began more than eight centuries of English involvement in Ireland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-norman-invasion-of-ireland.jpg" alt="Anglo-Norman invasion of Ireland" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Maclise · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MarriageAoifeStrongbow.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
